    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to bring No. 51 Seagrange Road to the market. This lovely three bedroomed terraced home which has had the attic converted. It is presented in great condition having been lovingly maintained and updated by the current owners. The property is facing a green and is absolutely ideal for family living.\n\nThis well-laid-out home offers well-planned and versatile accommodation across three floors. On the ground floor, there is a comfortable living room and a bright open-plan kitchen/dining room, ideal for everyday living and entertaining. The first floor comprises two generous double bedrooms, a single bedroom, and a modern family bathroom. The converted attic provides valuable additional space, perfect for a home office, playroom, or guest accommodation. Externally, the property benefits from off-street parking to the front and a private rear garden complete with an outhouse with electricity and further development. Enjoying an attractive position facing onto a green, this home offers a pleasant and family-friendly setting.\n\nLocation is excellent. Set in a quiet and friendly neighbourhood, facing a green in a well established, family-friendly development close to a whole host of amenities including selection of schools, shops, sports & leisure facilities. Good public transport links to and from Dublin City Centre with both bus and train. \n\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate this fine family home in a most convenient and highly sought-after location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - 0.5m x 1.8m\nGlass porch\n\nHall - 3.7m x 1.8m\nBright entrance hallway featuring wooden flooring and recessed lighting.\n\nLiving Room - 4.1m x 3.1m\nA front living room features wooden flooring, recessed lighting, and a TV point.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 4.58m x 5m\nThe kitchen features a painted shaker-style design with quartz countertops, solid wood cabinetry, and wooden flooring. Complete with a breakfast counter, integrated Belling gas hob, fridge/freezer, Belfast sink, and plumbed for a washing machine, it also opens to the rear garden through French doors.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - 5.73m x 1.74m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.8m x 2.63m\nA spacious double bedroom to the front, featuring wooden flooring and full-length fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 5.44m x 3.22m\nA bright double bedroom to the rear, featuring wooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.0m x 2.3m\nA single bedroom to the front, featuring wooden flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.83m x 1.73m\nThe bathroom features a WC, wash hand basin, tiled bath with shower, and wooden flooring.\n\nSecond Floor - \n\n\nAttic - 5.0m x 4.67m\nThe attic features a Velux window and wooden flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.36m x 1.69m\nThe bathroom features a WC, wash hand basin, Velux window and tiled flooring.\n\nOutside - \n\n\nFront Garden - \nThe front garden is walled, paved, and gated, with off-street parking and overlooks the green.\n\nRear Garden - \nPrivate rear garden with a paved patio and a generous shed with electricity\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>3 bed, 2 terraced house </li><li>Excellent location</li><li>Insulated c.2023</li><li>Gas Fired Central Heating</li><li>uPVC Double Glazed windows </li><li>Off street parking</li><li>Overlooking the green</li><li>Attic Conversion</ul>"
      },
